26
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on Knot]

27
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,820
I will be more careful in the future.

28
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,500
Then you won't have to
suffer.

29
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:53,740
-Go with him, Ongsa.
-Look at Nakhin.

30
00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:56,030
He probably wants you to go back with him.

31
00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:00,410
I really don't get why you insisted on
taking me here.

32
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:02,370
Drop me back at the café.

33
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,210
Because I want you to come.

34
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:07,080
What for?

35
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:11,230
Because I want to
be around the person I like.

36
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,260
You're talking nonsense again.

37
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,140
I mean every word.

38
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,170
You always like to talk nonsense.

39
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,940
I'm not making anything up.

40
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,450
I'm serious about
taking things further with you.

41
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:28,500
I don't know either.

42
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,440
I've never dated an Alpha before.

43
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:33,329
So that means...

44
00:02:33,350 --> 00:02:35,900
I'm your first?

45
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:38,480
I mean, my first Alpha.

46
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,250
Still counts as your first.

47
00:02:46,579 --> 00:02:47,940
Ongsa,

48
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:52,600
see me just as a man who's fallen for you,

49
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:55,840
who wants to stay by your side,

50
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,829
and who hopes
you might return his feelings.

51
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:02,940
Don't let other things
cloud your judgment, okay?

52
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:04,750
But you...

53
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:07,230
You look like a total flirt.

54
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,080
Me?

55
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,830
Yeah.

56
00:03:11,690 --> 00:03:14,050
You look like a smooth talker.

57
00:03:15,170 --> 00:03:16,780
And...

58
00:03:17,090 --> 00:03:19,440
You know exactly how to soften people up.

59
00:03:19,690 --> 00:03:21,740
That's just charisma.

60
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,560
Really?

61
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:25,740
If you're worried I'm a playboy,

62
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,440
then take more time to observe me.

63
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,690
How about this?

64
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,940
I'll put you on probation first.

65
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,570
If you pass the test,
I'll give you an official title.

66
00:03:36,130 --> 00:03:37,810
Isn't that a little harsh?

67
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,120
It's not harsh.

68
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:40,980
It's being cautious.

69
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,840
Then what title sits somewhere
above just friends?

70
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:48,120
For now,

71
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:51,100
I guess we're flirt buddies.

72
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:54,550
What's so special about that?

73
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:56,900
We're chatting right now, aren't we?

74
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,130
It's different.

75
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:03,440
Because I only chat like this

76
00:04:05,090 --> 00:04:06,890
with you.

77
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,540
Hi, bro.

78
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:32,860
Did you get the medicine?

79
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:34,220
Yes, I got it.

80
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,740
I'm with Ongsa right now.

81
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:38,490
We just dropped Saengnuea off.

82
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,440
Hurry over here, then.

83
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:41,990
Got it, bro.

84
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,150
Hey,

85
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:48,470
can we take the medicine
to my brother first?

86
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:49,220
What?

87
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:52,000
My brother got shot.

88
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,110
We need to get this to him quickly.

89
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:56,390
Didn't you just tell Phatsa

90
00:04:56,409 --> 00:04:58,940
that True Alphas
have strong constitutions?

91
00:04:59,290 --> 00:05:01,290
I'm sure he'll be fine.

92
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,570
So does this "flirt buddy" title mean

93
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,080
you can come over to my place?

94
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,200
Come with me.

95
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,360
Phatsa will be happy to see you.

96
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:25,020
Thank you.

97
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:30,610
Thank you.

98
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,610
Sigh.

99
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,600
Let me serve you some rice.

100
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,810
Mm-hmm.

101
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:42,890
Remember to take the medicine
after the meal.

102
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,520
I want the curry you made yesterday.

103
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:54,130
I dumped all of it for the dog.

104
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:55,190
What?

105
00:05:58,159 --> 00:05:59,960
But that was supposed to be mine.

106
00:06:04,370 --> 00:06:06,480
It's an impressive place, right?

107
00:06:07,890 --> 00:06:10,010
It's amazing.

108
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,240
Here's the food.

109
00:06:18,330 --> 00:06:19,790
This is the Massaman curry

110
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:22,180
Phatsa cooked last night.

111
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:27,350
Excuse me.

112
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:35,950
Didn't you say you gave it to the dog?

113
00:06:39,790 --> 00:06:43,120
That's exactly this bowl.
Aren't you always biting people?

114
00:06:45,830 --> 00:06:46,909
Thank you.

115
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,300
My pleasure, Mr. Phatsa.

116
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,360
Enjoy your meal.

117
00:06:51,270 --> 00:06:52,600
I never knew

118
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:54,770
Phatsa could cook,

119
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:56,700
especially such a complicated dish.

120
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,460
Ongsa, cut it out.

121
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,860
Normally, you could even burn a pot

122
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:02,850
just trying to cook instant noodles

123
00:07:02,850 --> 00:07:04,840
Ongsa...

124
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,420
Actually, this curry

125
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,120
was made by Nakhun's mom.

126
00:07:11,590 --> 00:07:13,890
I only helped a little.

127
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,060
Look.

128
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,010
I cut my finger

129
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,710
chopping potatoes.

130
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:30,390
But,

131
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,530
Ongsa,

132
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,240
you're great at cooking.

133
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,290
Your cakes are delicious,

134
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:39,200
especially

135
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:40,960
banana cheesecake.

136
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,110
It's the best cake in the world.

137
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:44,610
Really?

138
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:47,050
Phatsa is exaggerating.

139
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,130
By the way,

140
00:07:49,159 --> 00:07:50,700
Nakhin,

141
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,590
is there anything
you especially like to eat?

142
00:07:52,590 --> 00:07:54,210
You don't need to know.

143
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:02,820
What?

144
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:05,580
What's wrong now?

145
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,990
I was just

146
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,690
asking casually.

147
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:15,960
Maybe someone here wants to know.

148
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:28,630
Hi, Mr. Naphitch.

149
00:08:31,030 --> 00:08:32,559
Come

150
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,250
and eat with us.

151
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,030
I'm not hungry.

152
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:56,810
Why

153
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,580
did you two do that?

154
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:01,000
What did I do?

155
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,180
Why did you two

156
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:06,580
look at your brother like that?

157
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,260
He's your sibling.

158
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:13,880
Can't you eat together peacefully?

159
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,150
As an outsider,

160
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,710
if you treat me like that,

161
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,260
I wouldn't want to stay here either.

162
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:36,060
It feels so stifling.

163
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:37,960
But this is different.

164
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:42,550
Forget it.

165
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,690
I was just saying.

166
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,990
Maybe you two can understand.

167
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,080
He's your sibling.

168
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:52,520
Be a little nicer to him.

169
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,100
It's not that hard.

170
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,720
OK, let's dig in.

171
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:05,630
Come on.

172
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:14,160
Wow, what a strange family.

173
00:11:18,070 --> 00:11:20,050
You have ridiculous pride.

174
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,090
If I were you just now,

175
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:50,830
I would never have walked away.

176
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,770
I would make them see exactly

177
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:58,480
how capable I am.

178
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,930
I'm just saying.

179
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:15,160
It's nothing.

180
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:22,870
That's it.

181
00:12:51,390 --> 00:12:52,780
What's wrong?

182
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,750
I know

183
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:03,950
you're still scared deep down.

184
00:13:04,470 --> 00:13:06,060
You scared that one day

185
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,050
I'll think you are inferior to others,

186
00:13:09,850 --> 00:13:11,910
or I'll grow tired of you,

187
00:13:13,310 --> 00:13:14,640
because you feel

188
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:18,030
you don't belong
where the world thinks you should be.

189
00:13:21,090 --> 00:13:22,290
But listen to me.

190
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:26,000
I chase you because you are Ongsa.

191
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:29,270
If you were an Alpha,

192
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:31,740
I would still choose you.

193
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:34,310
If you were an Omega,

194
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:36,790
I would still choose you.

195
00:13:37,350 --> 00:13:40,010
If everyone in the world
turns their back on you,

196
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:43,970
I will still walk toward you.

197
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:50,090
Because in the end,

198
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,770
the person I truly want standing beside me

199
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:54,970
is no one else but you,

200
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:05,450
Ongsa.

201
00:14:15,350 --> 00:14:17,280
You're still such a smooth talker.

202
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,640
I'm not smooth-talking.

203
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:22,940
Every word I say
comes straight from my heart.

204
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:26,730
It's getting late.

205
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:29,090
You should head back.

206
00:14:29,730 --> 00:14:32,610
But I will keep chasing you tomorrow.

207
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,910
Who said you could chase me?

208
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,580
I don't plan to ask for your permission.

209
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,180
I've already made up my mind.

210
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:53,230
About that land bid
we talked about before,

211
00:14:53,230 --> 00:14:55,760
which area do you think
is worth looking into?

212
00:14:56,350 --> 00:14:58,620
There's one plot
worth paying attention to

213
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:00,080
in Chachoengsao.

214
00:15:00,110 --> 00:15:02,480
Right now, it's land with no road access.

215
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:05,800
But I heard the government
plans to expropriate land

216
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:08,010
and build a new ring road.

217
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:10,310
Where does it lead?

218
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,980
From Laem Chabang
to Suvarnabhumi,

219
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,050
extending to Bang Na,

220
00:15:15,070 --> 00:15:16,870
then connecting to Khlong Toei.

221
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:19,110
If that happens,

222
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,520
the value of that area

223
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:22,310
will soar in the future.

224
00:15:22,750 --> 00:15:24,990
It's perfect for building warehouses

225
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:27,230
or developing logistics businesses.

226
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:29,920
Have you inspected the site in person?

227
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,300
Not yet.

228
00:15:31,730 --> 00:15:33,720
I plan to go next week.

229
00:15:34,230 --> 00:15:36,620
In that case,

230
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:39,310
take Nakhin and Naphitch with you.

231
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,850
Let Naphitch learn more practical work.

232
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,350
Yes, Father.

233
00:15:45,710 --> 00:15:46,510
OK.

234
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:49,180
Go out, see, listen and learn.

235
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,710
For this kind of work,

236
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,330
you truly understand
only when you see it with your own eyes.

237
00:15:53,330 --> 00:15:54,060
Understood.

238
00:15:55,610 --> 00:15:56,620
Nakhun,

239
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:59,940
how's your plan
for your birthday banquet this year?

240
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:04,760
Work has been quite busy recently,

241
00:16:04,850 --> 00:16:06,270
so I was thinking

242
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:09,840
we shouldn't make it too grand this year.

243
00:16:11,030 --> 00:16:12,630
We still have to throw a party

244
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:15,020
because it's not just a birthday party.

245
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:17,310
It also affects

246
00:16:17,730 --> 00:16:19,260
the industry's confidence

247
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:20,510
in our family.

248
00:16:20,530 --> 00:16:21,940
Especially this year,

249
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:23,880
we have to make it decent

250
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:26,770
to show that our family is still stable.

251
00:16:29,710 --> 00:16:33,030
Alright, we will do as Mom and Dad wish.

252
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,730
Phatsa,

253
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:40,210
if I ask you to help organize
Nakhun's birthday banquet, can you help?

254
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,580
Sure,

255
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,220
I'll give it a try.

256
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:51,600
I'll tell you
the specific arrangements later.

257
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:52,320
Okay.

258
00:16:53,560 --> 00:16:55,010
If we split the land

259
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:57,080
into smaller plots and sell separately,

260
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,520
will profits be higher?

261
00:16:58,730 --> 00:17:00,200
Of course they will.

262
00:17:00,790 --> 00:17:04,109
We can earn an extra 200 to 300 thousand
baht per plot.

263
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:05,140
There are two ways

264
00:17:06,619 --> 00:17:08,240
to develop this land.

265
00:17:09,829 --> 00:17:11,720
If you want a higher selling price,

266
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:14,520
the first option
is subdividing the land for sale.

267
00:17:15,569 --> 00:17:17,060
And the second option...

268
00:17:23,770 --> 00:17:24,750
Hey,

269
00:17:25,099 --> 00:17:26,990
if you don't take this seriously,

270
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:31,130
don't complain later about losing money.

271
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,540
Sorry.

272
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,850
Let's continue.

273
00:17:46,850 --> 00:17:47,750
And

274
00:17:48,450 --> 00:17:49,960
the second option is,

275
00:17:50,350 --> 00:17:52,370
if we don't want to
wait for buyers to come to us,

276
00:17:52,370 --> 00:17:54,090
we can develop the land ourselves

277
00:17:54,090 --> 00:17:55,890
and build real estate projects.

278
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,370
Hmm, I think that's a good idea.

279
00:17:59,190 --> 00:18:00,620
By the way,

280
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,540
can I invite Ongsa to help

281
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,830
with your birthday banquet?

282
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:07,530
He runs a café,

283
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:09,880
so he should be much better at this
than me.

284
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,770
Of course.

285
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,890
My brother will be happy too.

286
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:18,990
You think the same as me, right?

287
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,280
Ongsa just loves pretending.

288
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,380
He always says

289
00:18:27,730 --> 00:18:29,080
he's only a Beta.

290
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,230
It's no surprise

291
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:34,580
he thinks that way.

292
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:37,040
In a world of Alphas and Omegas,

293
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:39,280
Betas are like outsiders.

294
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,830
What if I were a Beta?

295
00:18:47,790 --> 00:18:50,050
Then we probably wouldn't be soulmates.

296
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,010
We might not have even met.

297
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,230
Nakhun,

298
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:18,440
help me check these documents.

299
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:46,630
I heard a Pure Omega went to the hospital
for an examination, is that correct?

300
00:19:46,630 --> 00:19:47,710
Yes, sir.

301
00:19:48,070 --> 00:19:49,640
But the patient's information

302
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:52,650
has been classified as confidential,
and the identity won't be revealed.

303
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:53,780
Confidential?

304
00:19:58,770 --> 00:20:00,210
Find out who it is.

305
00:20:00,530 --> 00:20:01,850
At all costs,

306
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:04,260
I want to know who that kid is.

307
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:05,480
Yes, sir.

308
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:07,140
What a pity.

309
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:09,140
Nakhun has already formed a bond,

310
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:11,070
otherwise...

311
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,550
Are you talking to me?

312
00:20:13,610 --> 00:20:14,940
I'm talking to myself.

313
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,110
Sorry.

314
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:20,190
If we want the child born
to have a chance to become an Enigma,

315
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:26,400
the Pure Omega must be paired with Nakhin.

316
00:20:27,470 --> 00:20:28,820
Are you still talking to yourself?

317
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:29,960
I'm asking you!

318
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:32,200
Ah, I'm sorry.

319
00:20:32,750 --> 00:20:35,860
I'll have someone
handle it right away, sir.

320
00:20:47,410 --> 00:20:52,160
There's a strange smell
in the air around here.

321
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,380
Smells like rotten oranges.

322
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:57,150
Let those who can truly smell it hate it.

323
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:58,710
People

324
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:00,170
who can't sense pheromones

325
00:21:00,170 --> 00:21:01,850
are just ordinary folks.

326
00:21:01,870 --> 00:21:03,520
Ordinary folks?

327
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:05,030
Word is,

328
00:21:05,050 --> 00:21:08,170
a powerful high-status family

329
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:12,700
brought an unknown Omega
into their household.

330
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,310
People say
whatever pops into their heads,

331
00:21:15,330 --> 00:21:17,210
like they are possessed.

332
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:19,810
-Excuse...
-What?

333
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:32,370
Downstairs just now,

334
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:35,010
were you trying to bite me to death,

335
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:36,440
or teasing me on purpose?

336
00:21:37,430 --> 00:21:38,790
What about you?

337
00:21:39,210 --> 00:21:41,870
You started picking on me
the second you talked.

338
00:21:42,630 --> 00:21:44,500
When you meet someone you dislike,

339
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,230
you test them first, don't you?

340
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:50,120
How interesting.

341
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,610
That's all because
your mother doesn't like our family.

342
00:21:52,610 --> 00:21:55,250
Your father chose not to marry my mother.

343
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:58,030
My mother never got over it
for some reason.

344
00:21:58,910 --> 00:22:02,490
In the end,
that man married another woman anyway.

345
00:22:02,510 --> 00:22:05,270
Hey, that man you're talking about
is my dad.

346
00:22:05,930 --> 00:22:08,860
Oops, sorry.

347
00:22:08,890 --> 00:22:11,540
Come on, a toast to my friend.

348
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:21,200
Would it be weird

349
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:23,430
if an Alpha falls for a Beta?

350
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:26,580
A Beta is still human,

351
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:28,860
with flesh, blood and a heart.

352
00:22:29,150 --> 00:22:32,140
So only if you fall for a dog or a ghost,

353
00:22:32,170 --> 00:22:33,660
you should think twice.

354
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,060
You have a sharp tongue.

355
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:36,700
But it's the truth, isn't it?

356
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:40,500
I've always thought this way though.

357
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:42,260
My best friend is a Beta.

358
00:22:43,050 --> 00:22:45,620
An outstanding, smart Beta girl.

359
00:22:45,640 --> 00:22:47,490
She's no worse than any Alpha.

360
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,630
Maybe you aren't clueless
about everything.

361
00:22:50,970 --> 00:22:52,840
Is that a compliment?

362
00:22:53,810 --> 00:22:55,160
Sort of.

363
00:22:57,980 --> 00:23:00,060
Sometimes I get fed up with my mom too.

364
00:23:02,150 --> 00:23:02,900
About what?

365
00:23:03,910 --> 00:23:04,930
Everything.

366
00:23:05,870 --> 00:23:08,340
She wants everything done exactly
as she plans.

367
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:10,020
Even the matter with Kingyok.

368
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:12,430
What's wrong with Kingyok?

369
00:23:12,930 --> 00:23:15,060
Actually, I have feelings for her too.

370
00:23:15,090 --> 00:23:16,740
But sometimes,

371
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:19,570
I feel like she never understands me.

372
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,450
I think

373
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,740
the problem

374
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:25,940
isn't only that
she doesn't understand you.

375
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:27,310
What do you mean?

376
00:23:27,330 --> 00:23:29,790
It's more like
you never give her the chance.

377
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:31,300
Most of the time,

378
00:23:32,090 --> 00:23:34,090
you only let her watch from far away,

379
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,760
like an outsider.

380
00:23:37,910 --> 00:23:40,110
If you want her to truly understand you,

381
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:43,340
you should let her
walk into your world more.

382
00:23:44,510 --> 00:23:47,350
You sound like you know everything.

383
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,610
Not everything, but on this matter,

384
00:23:51,320 --> 00:23:52,520
I see it very clearly.

385
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:55,910
Maybe you're right.

386
00:24:01,490 --> 00:24:02,560
I'm heading back.

387
00:24:03,190 --> 00:24:07,620
Come find me again

388
00:24:07,650 --> 00:24:10,240
if you want to discuss
cross-type relationships.

389
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,240
Thanks.

390
00:24:11,270 --> 00:24:12,670
This consultation isn't free though.

391
00:24:12,670 --> 00:24:13,740
Okay.

392
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:54,410
What's wrong, Kingyok?

393
00:25:15,450 --> 00:25:16,950
It's for you.

394
00:25:20,010 --> 00:25:20,780
No thanks.

395
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:24,560
Please drink it.

396
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:28,350
Thanks, but I really don't need it.

397
00:25:30,330 --> 00:25:32,420
-Hey.
-Hey.

398
00:25:33,110 --> 00:25:34,380
Are you okay?

399
00:25:35,540 --> 00:25:38,670
It spilled all over you.
I'm so sorry, it was an accident.

400
00:25:43,390 --> 00:25:44,160
It's fine.

401
00:25:44,970 --> 00:25:46,700
Just be more careful next time.

402
00:25:46,860 --> 00:25:48,990
Wait, I'll get a towel to wipe you down.

403
00:26:05,050 --> 00:26:06,320
Well,

404
00:26:07,870 --> 00:26:09,330
you can use this one.

405
00:26:15,950 --> 00:26:18,350
So many annoying things happened tonight.

406
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,120
Then

407
00:26:23,620 --> 00:26:25,280
don't let these little things

408
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,370
ruin your mood.

409
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,300
Let me sit with you for a while.

410
00:26:53,270 --> 00:26:54,330
That would be nice.

411
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:53,670
Mom, this is Ongsa.

412
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,900
I told you about him before.

413
00:27:56,310 --> 00:27:57,850
Hello, Auntie.

414
00:27:58,130 --> 00:27:59,910
Hello.

415
00:28:00,790 --> 00:28:02,800
You've grown into a handsome young man.

416
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:06,150
Just like your mother, gentle and likable.

417
00:28:06,180 --> 00:28:08,640
Send my regards to your mother.

418
00:28:08,670 --> 00:28:12,200
I still remember the banana cake she made.

419
00:28:12,220 --> 00:28:14,340
My mom passed the recipe to me.

420
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:15,570
Now,

421
00:28:15,590 --> 00:28:18,020
it's the signature dessert at my café.

422
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:20,650
I have to try it someday.

423
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,530
Mom will be overjoyed

424
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:26,140
if you visit.

425
00:28:26,170 --> 00:28:28,230
Omegas of your mother's generation

426
00:28:28,250 --> 00:28:29,830
are naturally skilled at

427
00:28:29,850 --> 00:28:31,960
making desserts.

428
00:28:31,980 --> 00:28:35,150
My mom often talks about you too.

429
00:28:35,180 --> 00:28:36,850
She said

430
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:39,700
you are especially good at
taking care of people around you.

431
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:42,390
Really?

432
00:28:42,410 --> 00:28:44,160
Well,

433
00:28:44,850 --> 00:28:46,850
you two keep chatting.

434
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:48,470
I need to use the restroom.

435
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:50,820
Okay, go ahead.

436
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,850
Does my dad

437
00:29:21,170 --> 00:29:22,010
know

438
00:29:23,620 --> 00:29:25,040
I'm an Omega?

439
00:29:28,460 --> 00:29:30,350
Or does he know nothing at all?

440
00:29:31,990 --> 00:29:33,720
Whether it's about the Alphas,

441
00:29:34,160 --> 00:29:35,230
Omegas,

442
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:38,780
or

443
00:29:41,300 --> 00:29:42,870
about me being bitten.

444
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:47,970
What if I had known all this
since I was little?

445
00:29:50,740 --> 00:29:52,400
What would things be like now?

446
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,610
Phatsa?

447
00:30:11,970 --> 00:30:12,800
Sign.

448
00:30:14,060 --> 00:30:16,270
Ongsa has gone back.

449
00:30:16,290 --> 00:30:18,460
Staff from the café called,

450
00:30:18,490 --> 00:30:20,750
asking him to rush back to handle orders.

451
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:23,970
Alright.

452
00:30:27,300 --> 00:30:32,150
Phatsa, can you help me pick some flowers?

453
00:30:34,320 --> 00:30:35,830
What kind of flowers?

454
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:40,510
I want to put some flowers
in Nakhun's room

455
00:30:40,530 --> 00:30:42,140
and the study.

456
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:46,050
I can't decide which ones to choose.

457
00:30:46,630 --> 00:30:48,970
Can you help me?

458
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:51,130
Sure.

459
00:30:51,770 --> 00:30:52,600
Good.

460
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:55,820
Do you like flower arranging?

461
00:30:56,510 --> 00:30:59,700
Yes, arranging flowers calms the mind

462
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:01,470
and lets me think.

463
00:31:02,060 --> 00:31:04,090
And Nakhun likes it too.

464
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:06,860
I often arrange bouquets
and put them in his room.

465
00:31:07,390 --> 00:31:08,470
Well,

466
00:31:09,590 --> 00:31:12,590
how about you try
arranging flowers for him sometime?

467
00:31:13,090 --> 00:31:14,890
I'm definitely not good enough.

468
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:18,120
I can't even pick
suitable flowers for you.

469
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:20,050
Besides,

470
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,720
Nakhun probably wouldn't care.

471
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:23,590
But

472
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:28,260
you two are soulmates.

473
00:31:28,280 --> 00:31:31,230
Normally,
soulmates understand each other deeply,

474
00:31:31,260 --> 00:31:34,750
or feel stronger attraction
than ordinary people.

475
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,450
I don't know.

476
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:43,300
If Nakhun and I weren't soulmates,

477
00:31:44,750 --> 00:31:47,190
we might never have met.

478
00:31:47,890 --> 00:31:49,930
Why do you think so, child?

479
00:31:51,860 --> 00:31:53,170
Nakhun said that.

480
00:31:53,620 --> 00:31:55,510
I can't believe Nakhun said that.

481
00:31:56,630 --> 00:31:58,000
Oh dear.

482
00:32:04,210 --> 00:32:05,640
Soulmates

483
00:32:06,310 --> 00:32:08,510
are no trivial matter, Phatsa.

484
00:32:08,530 --> 00:32:12,190
Thousands of people may never meet theirs.

485
00:32:12,210 --> 00:32:16,410
It's an extremely special fate
for Alphas and Omegas.

486
00:32:16,430 --> 00:32:19,910
It's not easy to come by.

487
00:32:20,590 --> 00:32:23,990
The fact that you met means
you are destined to have this fate.

488
00:32:25,630 --> 00:32:28,180
But what if we are destined to meet,

489
00:32:29,320 --> 00:32:30,840
yet never fall in love?

490
00:32:32,580 --> 00:32:34,930
Then fate is nothing more than a cage.

491
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:39,800
Don't rush to dismiss fate

492
00:32:40,310 --> 00:32:43,440
before love even begins.

493
00:33:04,680 --> 00:33:07,280
I think I told you everything
at the last meeting.

494
00:33:07,280 --> 00:33:08,820
See you at the hotel

495
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:10,430
when we meet next time.

496
00:33:11,020 --> 00:33:12,250
The hotel again.

497
00:33:13,140 --> 00:33:14,080
Okay.

498
00:33:19,250 --> 00:33:20,300
Eat on your own.

499
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:22,880
Where are you going, Mr. Phatsa?

500
00:33:23,750 --> 00:33:26,280
I'm really losing patience
with this family.

501
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:28,600
All they ever do is work.

502
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:32,570
They always have a stern face,
brows furrowed tight.

503
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:37,100
I wonder what they want
with all that power.

504
00:33:37,870 --> 00:33:39,930
Probably planning to rule the world.

505
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:43,580
Hmm.

506
00:33:44,510 --> 00:33:47,950
Phatsa, are you talking about Nakhun?

507
00:33:47,970 --> 00:33:50,450
He looks fierce,

508
00:33:50,990 --> 00:33:52,640
but he's actually so cool.

509
00:33:53,010 --> 00:33:54,380
Cool?

510
00:33:54,410 --> 00:33:55,970
He's just a dictator.

511
00:33:55,990 --> 00:33:58,350
Always mysterious,

512
00:33:58,670 --> 00:34:00,440
hiding secrets.

513
00:34:01,790 --> 00:34:03,320
He never tells me anything.

514
00:34:03,970 --> 00:34:06,500
Talking to him is like
talking to a brick wall.

515
00:34:07,250 --> 00:34:08,530
Alright, Phatsa.

516
00:34:09,300 --> 00:34:10,409
Calm down.

517
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:14,360
Maybe he's just swamped with work.

518
00:34:15,650 --> 00:34:18,550
Not like you, hiding here moping alone.

519
00:34:22,510 --> 00:34:23,670
Hi everyone.

520
00:34:24,469 --> 00:34:27,110
What are you all doing? It smells amazing.

521
00:34:28,270 --> 00:34:30,489
Want to try the banana cake

522
00:34:31,270 --> 00:34:32,540
I just baked?

523
00:34:32,560 --> 00:34:33,920
It's still warm.

524
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:36,360
It's so good,

525
00:34:36,860 --> 00:34:39,070
soft and fragrant, Ongsa.

526
00:34:39,090 --> 00:34:43,949
Can I learn the recipe from you maybe?

527
00:34:44,239 --> 00:34:45,730
I really can't give you

528
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,429
the recipe.

529
00:34:47,449 --> 00:34:49,260
It's my mom's exclusive recipe.

530
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:52,139
Actually, my mom's pheromone

531
00:34:52,159 --> 00:34:55,060
smells just like banana cake.

532
00:34:55,980 --> 00:34:57,080
I understand.

533
00:34:57,100 --> 00:35:00,480
Then I can be a regular customer
for this dessert.

534
00:35:00,510 --> 00:35:01,880
Of course.

535
00:35:03,770 --> 00:35:05,370
Is it really that delicious?

536
00:35:07,860 --> 00:35:08,640
Absolutely.

537
00:35:11,460 --> 00:35:12,570
Oh no.

538
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:15,630
Hey, come here.

539
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,320
What's wrong?

540
00:35:31,500 --> 00:35:32,230
How is it?

541
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,030
It smells like chili sauce.

542
00:35:46,860 --> 00:35:48,000
Nakhin.

543
00:35:48,300 --> 00:35:50,030
Nakhin, do you want to try this?

544
00:35:52,110 --> 00:35:52,990
Sure.

545
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:02,520
Is it good?

546
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:04,810
Extremely good.

547
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,220
Right?

548
00:36:06,290 --> 00:36:07,590
This uses

549
00:36:07,620 --> 00:36:10,250
Ongsa's mom's exclusive recipe.

550
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:13,270
No wonder

551
00:36:14,080 --> 00:36:15,820
it tastes amazing.

552
00:36:30,250 --> 00:36:32,360
Um... Nakhin, you carry on eating.

553
00:36:32,380 --> 00:36:34,620
I have to go. Something's up.

554
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:37,920
Ongsa, I'll take my leave.

555
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,020
OK...

556
00:36:48,510 --> 00:36:50,450
Always buried in work,

557
00:36:51,380 --> 00:36:53,230
face full of stress.

558
00:36:54,890 --> 00:36:56,890
His injury hasn't fully healed yet.

559
00:36:57,680 --> 00:36:59,830
Why rush so hard on projects?

560
00:37:00,690 --> 00:37:02,150
Phatsa,

561
00:37:02,930 --> 00:37:06,230
you've been complaining
about your partner for 10 minutes.

562
00:37:06,230 --> 00:37:08,340
He's not my partner.

563
00:37:09,030 --> 00:37:10,120
Okay,

564
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,330
he's not your partner,

565
00:37:12,830 --> 00:37:14,450
just your bonded match.

566
00:37:16,490 --> 00:37:17,830
You looking for a fight?

567
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:23,050
It's just such an awkward title.

568
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:25,960
